2026-09-27T07:22:14.4054079Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4054227Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4054446Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4054705Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4054775Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4054933Z ================
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4055025Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4055150Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4055432Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4055595Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4055680Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4055891Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4056021Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4056094Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4056282Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4056458Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4056782Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4057038Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4057094Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4057307Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4057575Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4057714Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4057884Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4058072Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4058118Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4058214Z ========
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4058267Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4058864Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4059486Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4059617Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4059854Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4060419Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4060708Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4060980Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4061191Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4061320Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4061477Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4061631Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4115857Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4116695Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4117716Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4118312Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4119025Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:22:14.4119216Z 
